{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:32720823 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:32720823 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"32720823","source":"MED","pmid":"32720823","pmcid":"PMC7388125","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC7388125"]},"doi":"10.1177/0300060520939832","title":"Effect of Low-dose ColchiciNe on the InciDence of Atrial Fibrillation in Open Heart Surgery Patients: END-AF Low Dose Trial.","authorString":"Tabbalat RA, Alhaddad I, Hammoudeh A, Khader YS, Khalaf HA, Obaidat M, Barakat J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Tabbalat RA","lastName":"Tabbalat","firstName":"Ramzi A","initials":"RA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2628-9618"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Abdali Clemenceau Hospital, Amman, Jordan."}]}},{"fullName":"Alhaddad I","lastName":"Alhaddad","firstName":"Imad","initials":"I","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Jordan Hospital, Amman, Jordan."}]}},{"fullName":"Hammoudeh A","lastName":"Hammoudeh","firstName":"Ayman","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Istishari Hospital, Amman, Jordan."}]}},{"fullName":"Khader YS","lastName":"Khader","firstName":"Yousef S","initials":"YS","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7830-6857"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Jordan University of Science and Technology, Irbid, Jordan."}]}},{"fullName":"Khalaf HA","lastName":"Khalaf","firstName":"Hassan Abu","initials":"HA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2166-6445"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Abdali Clemenceau Hospital, Amman, Jordan."}]}},{"fullName":"Obaidat M","lastName":"Obaidat","firstName":"Mohammad","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Abdali Clemenceau Hospital, Amman, Jordan."}]}},{"fullName":"Barakat J","lastName":"Barakat","firstName":"Jude","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Al Khalidi Hospital and Medical Center, Amman, Jordan."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7830-6857"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2166-6445"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2628-9618"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"7","volume":"48","journalIssueId":2974000,"dateOfPublication":"2020 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2020,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Int Med Res","title":"The Journal of international medical research","essn":"1473-2300","issn":"0300-0605","isoabbreviation":"J Int Med Res","nlmid":"0346411"},"printPublicationDate":"2020-07-01"},"pubYear":"2020","pageInfo":"300060520939832","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Studies using 1 mg of colchicine to prevent postoperative atrial fibrillation (POAF) reported conflicting results. Moreover, colchicine was associated with significant gastrointestinal (GI) side effects. This study examined whether low-dose colchicine effectively prevents POAF and whether low-dose therapy is associated with lower rates of colchicine-induced GI side effects.<h4>Methods</h4>In this prospective, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study, consecutive adult patients admitted for elective cardiac surgeries randomly received a 1-mg dose of colchicine (n = 81) or placebo (n = 71) orally 12 to 24 hours before surgery followed by a daily dose of 0.5 mg until hospital discharge. The primary efficacy endpoint was the development of at least one episode of POAF of ≥5 minutes. The primary safety endpoint was the development of adverse events, especially diarrhea.<h4>Results</h4>The in-hospital mortality rate was 3.9%. POAF occurred in 13 patients (16.1%) in the colchicine group and 13 patients (18.3%) in the placebo group (odds ratio 0.85 [95% Confidence Interval = 0.37-1.99]). Diarrhea occurred in two patients in each group and necessitated treatment discontinuation in one patient in each group.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Low-dose colchicine did not prevent POAF in patients undergoing cardiac surgery. These results should be interpreted cautiously because of the small sample size and early study termination.<b>ClinicalTrials.gov Unique Identifier number:</b> NCT03015831.","affiliation":"Abdali Clemenceau Hospital, Amman, Jordan.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Atrial Fibrillation","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Postoperative Complications","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PC","qualifierName":"prevention & control"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Colchicine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Treatment Outcome"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cardiac Surgical Procedures","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Incidence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Prospective Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adult"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Colchicine","Arrhythmia","Atrial fibrillation","Cardiac surgery","Randomized controlled trial","Gastrointestinal Toxicity"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Colchicine","registryNumber":"SML2Y3J35T"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[